---
layout: layouts/base.njk
permalink: "/contact.html"
title: "Tell us about your data | DataLeasers"
description: "Tell us about your data and DataLeasers will show whether it could be licensed for AI, through an introduction to the data buyer."
canonical: "https://dataleasers.com/contact.html"
navKey: contact
---
<main id="main">
  <section class="hero ink">
    <div class="wrap">
      <h1>Tell us about your data</h1>
      <p class="lead">Tell us a little about your company. We will reply to arrange a short conversation.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section mist">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="type-split">
        <div class="reveal">
      <p class="notice-ok" id="form-sent" hidden>Thank you. We will reply to arrange a call.</p>
      <p class="notice-err" id="form-error" hidden>Something went wrong, or a field was not valid. Please check and try again.</p>
      <form action="https://app.dataleasers.com/api/leads" method="post">
        <label>Name
          <input type="text" name="name" autocomplete="name" required maxlength="200">
        </label>
        <label>Work email
          <input type="email" name="email" autocomplete="email" required maxlength="320">
        </label>
        <label>Company
          <input type="text" name="company" autocomplete="organization" required maxlength="200">
        </label>
        <label>Your role
          <input type="text" name="role" maxlength="200">
        </label>
        <label>What kind of data does your company generate?
          <textarea name="data" maxlength="2000"></textarea>
        </label>
        <div class="hp" aria-hidden="true">
          <label>Leave this empty<input type="text" name="website" tabindex="-1" autocomplete="off"></label>
        </div>
        <p><button class="btn" type="submit">Tell us about your data</button></p>
      </form>
      <p class="muted small-note">We use these details only to reply to your enquiry. See <a href="trust.html">How we handle your data</a>.</p>
      <script>
        (function () {
          var q = new URLSearchParams(location.search);
          if (q.get('sent')) {
            document.getElementById('form-sent').hidden = false;
            /* Hide the form once it has been accepted, so nobody sends the
               same enquiry twice or wonders whether it went through. */
            document.querySelector('form[action$="/api/leads"]').hidden = true;
          }
          if (q.get('error')) document.getElementById('form-error').hidden = false;
        })();
      </script>
        </div>
        <aside class="signpost reveal">
          <h2>What happens next</h2>
          <ol class="next-steps">
            <li>We reply to arrange a short conversation.</li>
            <li>We look at which systems hold your records, and whether they fit what the data buyer looks for.</li>
            <li>If there is a fit, we make the introduction. Nothing is shared without your approval.</li>
          </ol>
          <p class="muted small-note">A first call commits you to nothing.</p>
        </aside>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section teal-soft">
    <div class="wrap">
      <h2 class="reveal">What to have ready</h2>
      <p class="reveal">Nothing formal. No NDA is needed for the first conversation, and no export is expected before it. If you can answer these three, the call will be useful.</p>
      <ul class="checklist reveal">
        <li><strong>Which tools hold the work</strong>Email, chat, file storage and CRM, plus the support or project tool your team runs on.</li>
        <li><strong>Roughly how far back they go</strong>Three years or more is the published floor, and those records have to still sit in the systems.</li>
        <li><strong>Who can approve</strong>The person able to agree that the company&rsquo;s records can be licensed, if the fit is there.</li>
      </ul>
      <p class="reveal">A no is a normal outcome and arrives on the first call rather than after months of review. The <a href="what-you-can-sell.html">published floors are here</a> if you would rather check them first.</p>
    </div>
  </section>
</main>
